`src/edit_apply.rs`, `src/edit_diagnostics.rs` and `src/edit_diff.rs` are copies
of `crates/rpi-tools/src/tools/{edit_apply,edit_diagnostics,edit_diff}.rs`, and
the tool description and parameter schema in `src/lib.rs` come from
`crates/rpi-tools/src/tools/edit.rs`. Each copied file keeps the source note in
its module docs. The only adaptations are crate-internal `use` paths and the
replacement of the host's `FileError`/`FileErrorCode` with the plugin-local
`FailureCode`, because a plugin reports failure text rather than a host error.

Ported candidate finder: pi-semantic-edit
-----------------------------------------

    pi-semantic-edit — https://github.com/k3-2o/pi-semantic-edit
    Copyright (c) 2026 K2
    Licensed under the MIT License.

`src/semantic_edit/` is the candidate-finding subset of `pi-semantic-edit`'s
domain layer (`src/domain/{passes,chain,closest,similarity}.ts`), taken from the
copy in `rpi` (`crates/rpi-tools/src/tools/semantic_edit/`). It only proposes
the regions a failure report quotes; it never decides that an edit matches.

